      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LET'S JUST SEE (1) goes very well at the distance with three wins and a placing from six starts. Recorded a 1.5 lengths win (24.96) in a Grade 5 last time at this track. Appeals as a leading chance in this. JUNEAU QUADRANT (2) failed to feature last start at Dubbo, but prior to that won by half a length at Launceston (30.45) beating Timeless Panama in a Maiden on September 28. Some good form is emerging from his last run. Better than last start and can bounce back. TRUST A PROCESS (8) had been super consistent recording two placings in a row before he was rewarded with a win last time, scoring at this track over 340m (19.94). Goes well out of this box with a win and two minor placings. Capable of going well again. JUNGLE TICKET (7) is worth a look over a shorter distance this time.",
